  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reductive ozonolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> followed by hydrolysis gives only one type of ketones because of symmetry across the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and bonding of two same alkyl groups <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math> with both the carbons bonded through double bond.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_598c90fb1297.png\" style=\"width: 526px; height: 167px;\" /></p>"
